2.4 Life-Cycle States
Asset states
State	Meaning	Allowed next states
Registered	Recorded, not yet in use or listed	In Use, Available
In Use	Allocated to a department	Available, Under Maintenance, Pending Disposition
Available	Published as surplus in the marketplace	Reserved, In Use, Under Maintenance, Pending Disposition
Reserved	Held for one request	In Transfer, Available
In Transfer	Approved and being moved	In Use
Under Maintenance	Inspection or repair open	In Use, Available, Pending Disposition
Pending Disposition	Donation, recycling or disposal proposed	Donated, Recycled, Disposed, In Use
Donated / Recycled / Disposed	Final states; record kept read-only	—
Request states: Draft → Submitted → Under Review → Approved or Rejected; Approved → Fulfilled; Submitted or Under Review → Cancelled (by requester) or Expired.
Transfer states: Scheduled → Dispatched → Received (confirmed by receiving custodian) → Completed; Scheduled or Dispatched → Cancelled; Dispatched → Disputed (damage or loss reported on arrival).
Maintenance states: Reported → Inspected → In Repair → Resolved; Inspected → Not Repairable (triggers a sustainability recommendation).
2.5 Operating Environment
Desktop and mobile web browsers (current Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox) on the university network or approved VPN. Server: FastAPI on a local or low-cost host, PostgreSQL 15 or later.
2.6 Assumptions and Dependencies
•	Representative sample data (departments, assets, requests) is acceptable for development and the demo.
•	Each asset has one owning department and one responsible custodian.
•	Gemini API access and a test key are available; if not, the matching engine falls back to rule-based search (FR-AI-9).
•	Carbon and waste factors for sustainability figures come from a published factor table agreed with the instructor [TBD-1].
3. External Interface Requirements
3.1 User Interfaces
A responsive web interface with a role-based dashboard, top navigation (Assets, Marketplace, Requests, Approvals, Maintenance, Reports, Assistant) and a help link on every screen. Error messages appear next to the field in red text with a plain explanation. AI suggestions are always shown with a confidence value, a reason and Accept / Edit / Dismiss buttons.
3.2 Hardware Interfaces
No special hardware. Users need a computer or phone with a browser; photos may come from a phone or laptop camera upload.
3.3 Software Interfaces
•	PostgreSQL 15+ database for all records (assets, users, requests, transfers, history).
•	Gemini API (classification, embeddings for matching, recommendations, assistant, report text), called only by the FastAPI backend.
•	Email (SMTP) service for notification copies.
3.4 Communications Interfaces
HTTPS (TLS 1.2+) between browser and server; JSON over a REST API between the React front end and FastAPI; HTTPS to the Gemini API with the key kept on the server.
