4.13 AI-Enhanced Features
4.13.1 Description and Priority
Five AI features advise users: classification, matching, sustainable-action recommendation, the assistant and generated reports. None makes a final decision. Priority: High (required by the project brief), built after the core workflow.
4.13.2 Stimulus/Response Sequences
•	User enters an asset name and description → system suggests a category and tags.
•	Requester submits a need → system shows the top 5 matches with scores and reasons.
•	Asset is marked Not Repairable or proposed for end of life → system recommends an action.
•	User types a question → assistant answers within the user's permissions.
•	AI Service does not answer within 10 seconds → system falls back to rule-based results.
4.13.3 Functional Requirements
ID	Requirement	Priority
FR-AI-1	Classification. When a user enters an asset's name and description, the system shall suggest a category, subcategory, up to 8 tags, material type and a standard description.	M
FR-AI-2	The system shall show each classification suggestion with a confidence value and shall save it only after the user accepts or edits it.	M
FR-AI-3	The system shall list fields the AI finds missing (e.g. no model number) as prompts to the user.	C
FR-AI-4	Matching. The system shall compare a request with available assets by meaning, not only exact keywords.	M
FR-AI-5	Before scoring, the system shall exclude assets that fail hard rules: not Available, quantity too low, or condition below the requested minimum.	M
FR-AI-6	The system shall give each asset–request pair a compatibility score from 0 to 1 using category, purpose, specifications, quantity, condition, location, urgency, required date, transfer cost and repair cost.	M
FR-AI-7	The system shall show the top 5 matches ranked by score, each with a plain-language reason naming its 2–3 main factors.	M
FR-AI-8	The system shall rank matches with equal suitability higher when they give more waste diversion or carbon reduction.	S
FR-AI-9	If the AI service fails or times out after 10 seconds, then the system shall fall back to rule-based keyword search and tell the user AI ranking is unavailable.	M
FR-AI-10	Sustainable action. The system shall recommend one of: retain, transfer, repair, refurbish, donate, disassemble for parts, recycle or dispose, with a reason and confidence.	M
FR-AI-11	The system shall never change an asset's state from an AI recommendation without an authorised user's approval.	M
FR-AI-12	If a recommendation's confidence is below 0.6, then the system shall label it "Low confidence – review carefully".	S
FR-AI-13	Assistant. The system shall let users ask questions in English (Arabic: C) to search assets, start a request, check status, view asset history and get policy guidance.	M
FR-AI-14	The assistant shall only return data and run actions the user is permitted to see or do, using the same permission checks as the normal screens.	M
FR-AI-15	Before the assistant submits a request on the user's behalf, the system shall show a summary and require the user to confirm.	M
FR-AI-16	Generative reports. The system shall produce a monthly narrative report on exchanges, maintenance trends, avoided purchases, savings, waste diversion, carbon reduction, high-demand categories and suggested actions.	M
FR-AI-17	Every number in a generated report shall come from database totals computed by the system; the AI writes only the narrative.	M
FR-AI-18	The system shall let any user override or dismiss an AI suggestion, and shall record the override (FR-AUD-4).	M
4.14 Sustainability Measurement
4.14.1 Description and Priority
Measures the environmental and financial value of reuse. Priority: Medium.
4.14.2 Stimulus/Response Sequences
•	Transfer completes → system asks whether it replaced a planned purchase.
•	Sustainability officer opens the dashboard → system shows savings, waste diverted, CO2e and reuse rate by department and month.
4.14.3 Functional Requirements
ID	Requirement	Priority
FR-SUS-1	When a request is fulfilled by reuse, the system shall ask whether it replaced a planned purchase and record that as an avoided purchase.	M
FR-SUS-2	The system shall compute financial savings as the estimated replacement cost of avoided purchases minus transfer and repair costs (AED).	M
FR-SUS-3	The system shall compute waste diverted (kg) from each reused, repaired, donated or recycled asset, using a weight per category.	S
FR-SUS-4	The system shall estimate carbon reduction (kg CO2e) using an emission factor per category from the agreed factor table [TBD-1], shown as an estimate with its source.	S
FR-SUS-5	The system shall compute reuse rate (fulfilled-by-reuse requests ÷ all fulfilled requests) and asset-life extension (years added by reuse or repair).	S
FR-SUS-6	The system shall show these indicators on a dashboard by department and month.	M
